 ### Visits
 
-<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a>
+<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a><a id="req-vis-003"></a>
 
-A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
+A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`. A visit booked in error — for the wrong pet or the wrong day — can be cancelled from the owner's record. Each upcoming visit — one whose date is later than today — carries a cancel action beside it on the owner detail page. A past visit carries none. Cancelling permanently removes that visit from the pet's record, so it no longer appears under the pet. The clinic keeps no visit lifecycle state, so a cancelled visit is not retained in a cancelled state — the record is gone `[REQ-VIS-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a pet with an upcoming visit (date later than today), when the owner detail page is shown, then a cancel action appears beside that visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a pet with a past visit (date today or earlier), when the owner detail page is shown, then no cancel action appears beside that visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given an upcoming visit, when its cancel action is invoked, then the visit is removed from the pet's record, and the owner detail page shown afterward no longer lists it while the pet's other visits remain.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. `[REQ-VIS-003]` Cancelling a visit that does not belong to the named owner's pet is refused, and so is cancelling a visit whose date is today or earlier — the cancel path guards the upcoming-visit boundary rather than trusting the page to have hidden the action.
+4. `[REQ-VIS-003]` **Assumption stated, not derived.** "Upcoming" is defined as a date strictly later than today, the same boundary `REQ-VIS-001` accepts when booking; a visit whose date has arrived (today) or passed is a past visit and cannot be cancelled. This request adds cancelling only — amending or rescheduling a booked visit remains out of scope (NG-5).
 
